              "text": "أنزل — anzala — \"to unload; to bring down\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أنزل أبي الأمتعة من القطار. anzala abī al-amtiʿa min al-qiṭār. My father unloaded the luggage from the train."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Present: ينزل, yunzil."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Unvocalized, its present ينزل looks like that of nazala, \"to go down\" (yanzil)."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "أنزل (anzala) is built on the native Arabic root n-z-l, \"to come down, to alight\" (Lane). It is Form IV, \"to bring down\"."
            }
          ]
        },
